         <div type="edition" xml:lang="pra-Latn" rendition="class:83225 maturity:83209">
             <p><lb n="1"/>Ayo ce<unclear>dana</unclear>vaniyo <space/> muḍakaseṭhikumārā ca</p>
         </div>
         <div type="apparatus">
             <listApp>
                 <app loc="1">
                     <lem>muḍakaseṭhikumārā</lem>
                     <rdg source="bib:Nakanishi+Hinuber2014_01">muḍakasaṭhikumārā</rdg>
                     <note>Understand <foreign>-kumāro</foreign>. This name is echoed in the Dīpavaṁsa 8:10, as <foreign>Mūlakadeva</foreign>. Note also that <foreign>Mūḍaka</foreign> (or perhaps rather <foreign>Mūḷaka</foreign>) as a place name is referred to in <ref target="DHARMA_INSKnI00406.xml">KnI 406</ref>. <bibl><ptr target="bib:Sarma+VaraPrasadaRao1993_01"/><citedRange unit="page">67-68</citedRange></bibl> situate this toponym in Western Maharashtra.</note>
                 </app>
             </listApp>
         </div>
         <div type="translation" resp="part:vito">
             <p>The Noble Cedana, a merchant and (the Noble?) Muḍaka, the son of a guild’s chief.</p>
         </div>
